    "answer": {
      "short": "$e(1)=2.00$, $e(10)=2.59$, $e(100)=2.70$, $e(1000)=2.72$, $e(10\\,000)=2.72$.\n\nThe values increase towards approximately $2.72$ as $x$ gets large.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}e(1)&=\\left(1+\\frac{1}{1}\\right)^1=2.00\\\\e(10)&=\\left(1+\\frac{1}{10}\\right)^{10}\\approx2.59\\\\e(100)&=\\left(1+\\frac{1}{100}\\right)^{100}\\approx2.70\\\\e(1000)&=\\left(1+\\frac{1}{1000}\\right)^{1000}\\approx2.72\\\\e(10\\,000)&=\\left(1+\\frac{1}{10\\,000}\\right)^{10\\,000}\\approx2.72\\end{align*}$$\nAll values are given to two decimal places. As $x$ gets large, the outputs increase and approach a fixed value of approximately $2.72$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
